hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1490","Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, h Al-Dawrqi narrated to us, and Salam bin Junada narrated to us, they said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash Al-Dawraqi said, he said: Al-A’mash told us, Bundar and Abu Musa told us, they said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, h Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari, our name is Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Dhakwan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The prayer of one of you in a group is twenty-few times greater than his prayer alone in his home and in his market. This is because if one of you performs ablution and performs it well, then goes out to pray, not wanting to do anything else, he does not take a step without God raising him up because of it. degree, and absolved him of a sin thereby.” This is the hadith of Bundar, and Abu Musa said: Or absolved him of it, and Bishr ibn Khalid said, and Salam ibn Junada, and Al-Duraqi: and he descended from him, and Al-Duraqi said: until he enters the mosque."
